course: dictionary
lesson: 14694
title: Stopping problems before they start
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Something preventative is meant to stop a bad thing from happening before it starts. Pre- means before, and prevent means to stop something happening. «Brushing your teeth every day is a preventative habit.» Brushing stops tooth problems before they begin, so preventative means stopping trouble early.
explain: Preventative can also be a noun. «The doctor gave her a preventative against flu.» Here a preventative is a medicine or treatment used to stop a problem. You can count them: one preventative, two preventatives.
explain: Some phrases use this word often. «Preventative medicine» keeps you well, «preventative measures» are steps taken early to stop trouble, and «preventive» means exactly the same as «preventative».
fact: Preventative means meant to stop something bad from happening before it starts.
fact: As a noun, a preventative is something used to stop a problem, such as a medicine or a treatment.
fact: «Preventative care» means checkups and treatments that keep you healthy, such as visits to the dentist.
fact: «Preventive» is another spelling that means the same as «preventative».
fact: The word part pre- means before, and prevent means to stop something from happening.
exercise: «Eating vegetables every day is a preventative habit.» What does preventative mean here? | *Meant to stop illness before it starts | Meant to make you feel sleepy | Meant to be eaten slowly | Meant to be very tasty
exercise: «The garage checked my bike as a preventative.» What is a preventative in this sentence? | A broken wheel | A type of road | *Something used to stop a problem before it happens | A fast bike that wins races
exercise: Which phrase means steps taken early to stop trouble? | *Preventative measures | Happy preventative | Loud measures | Preventative cake
test: «She took a preventative every winter.» Which word is the noun in this sentence? | *preventative | took | winter | every
test: «Preventative care» means which of these? | Looking after a pet that is sick | Care that is very loud and fast | *Checkups and treatments that keep you healthy | Carefully wrapping a present
exam: Which sentence uses preventative correctly? | The race was preventative and very fast | *Checking the brakes is a preventative step that stops accidents | Her preventative was a loud song | The old tree was a preventative, very tall and green
